L1 measures Little's law with real threads: a 200-thread pool takes 10.1 s for work that virtual threads finish in 0.55 s.

10
00:00:37.172 --> 00:00:52.809
L2 runs real HTTP services for three failures: a slow dependency without timeouts takes down an unrelated endpoint (20 or 500 OK versus 500 or 500 with a timeout and fallback);.

11
00:00:54.159 --> 00:01:06.789
fixed per-hop timeouts waste 89 seconds of work after users have already given up, while propagated deadlines waste none;. retries at every layer hit a failing leaf 27x versus 3x.

12
00:01:07.069 --> 00:01:18.034
